## 6. Connection String

```bash
az sql db show-connection-string \
  --server "$SQL_SERVER" \
  --name "$SQL_DB" \
  --client sqlcmd
```

Example:

```text
sqlcmd -S tcp:lab08-sql-74518410.database.windows.net,1433 -d lab08-db -U <username> -P <password> -N -l 30
```

I also connected using Azure Portal Query Editor and confirmed:

```sql
SELECT DB_NAME();
```

Result:

```text
lab08-db
```

### Important note

The Query Editor test confirmed:

```text
Azure Portal → Azure SQL Database
```

It did **not** prove that my physical PC connected through the firewall.

