## 10. Disable Public Network Access

```bash
az sql server update \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --name "$SQL_SERVER" \
  --set publicNetworkAccess=Disabled
```

Verify:

```bash
az sql server show \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --name "$SQL_SERVER" \
  --query publicNetworkAccess \
  -o tsv
```

Result:

```text
Disabled
```

### Result

Public Internet access to the SQL Server is disabled.

Access should now use the private network path through the Private Endpoint.

---

## 11. Backup

```bash
az sql db show \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --server "$SQL_SERVER" \
  --name "$SQL_DB" \
  --query "{backupRedundancy:currentBackupStorageRedundancy,tier:currentServiceObjectiveName,status:status}" \
  -o table
```

Result:

```text
backupRedundancy    tier    status
Geo                 Basic   Online
```

### What I learned

Azure manages the backup infrastructure for Azure SQL Database.

The customer still needs to understand and configure relevant backup, retention, and redundancy settings.

---

## 12. Availability

```bash
az sql db show \
  --resource-group "$RG" \
  --server "$SQL_SERVER" \
  --name "$SQL_DB" \
  --query "{tier:currentServiceObjectiveName,zoneRedundant:zoneRedundant,readScale:readScale}" \
  -o table
```

Result:

```text
tier    zoneRedundant    readScale
Basic   False            Disabled
```

### What I learned

`zoneRedundant=False` does not mean Azure SQL has no availability management.

Azure manages the underlying PaaS platform, while advanced availability features depend on the selected service tier/configuration.

---

# Key Takeaways

### IaaS vs PaaS

```text
IaaS:

VM
 ├── OS
 ├── SQL Server
 └── Database

Customer manages more infrastructure.
```

```text
PaaS:

Azure SQL Logical Server
        │
        └── Database

Azure manages the underlying platform.
```

### Private access

```text
Private Client
     ↓
Private DNS
     ↓
10.8.1.4
     ↓
Private Endpoint
     ↓
SQL Logical Server
     ↓
lab08-db
```

### Public access

```text
Internet
   X
SQL Server

Public Network Access = Disabled
```

